# Third-party notices

## Superpowers

Some skills in `plugins/clankit-dev/skills/` are derived from the Superpowers
plugin (https://github.com/obra/superpowers), used under the MIT License.

Vendored verbatim:

- `dispatching-parallel-agents`
- `receiving-code-review`
- `verification-before-completion`

Vendored with modifications:

- `brainstorming` — terminal state, trigger, domain scoping, companion branding
- `systematic-debugging` — skill references rewired; skill-development
  artifacts (creation log, pressure tests) dropped
- `writing-skills` — skill references rewired; other-harness paths removed
- `writing-good-tests` — promoted from a reference document inside
  `test-driven-development` to a skill of its own, with frontmatter added
- `writing-plans` — rewritten around a reduced task format
- `executing-plans` — merged with `subagent-driven-development`; its prompt
  templates and the `review-package` / workspace scripts are vendored with it

See `MAINTENANCE.md` for what each modification changes and why.

